WEBVTT

00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:11.240
(soft rattling)

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:13.840
(Lally) Newt.

00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:16.960
(Newt) Ah.

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:29.120
Albus. (panting)

00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:35.600
Theseus has been taken
to the Erkstag.

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:38.040
Wait, no, but the Erkstag
shut down years ago.

00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:42.600
Yes, well, it's the Ministry's
secret little bed and breakfast
now.

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:45.160
You'll need this to see him.

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:47.600
-And one of these. -(Jacob grunts)

00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:51.400
-(Jacob) Mm-hmm. -And this.

00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:54.800
(gateway rattling)

00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:56.480
Wait, wait, wait.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:00.280
I trust you're enjoying
your wand, Mr.

00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:01.080
Kowalski?

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:04.120
Me? Oh, uh... Yeah, thank you, Mr.
Dumbledore.

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:05.520
It's a real pip.

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:06.800
I advise you to keep it close.

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:08.560
-Professor Hicks. -Dumbledore.

00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:11.920
Assuming you're not otherwise
engaged, and frankly even if you
are,

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:14.560
I encourage you to attend
tonight's candidates' dinner.

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:16.120
Take Mr. Kowalski.

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:18.240
I'm quite certain there'll
be an assassination attempt.

00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:21.480
Anything you can do to scotch
that will be greatly appreciated.

00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:22.480
It's my pleasure.

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:23.920
I shall welcome the challenge.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:26.360
Besides, I'll have Jacob with me.

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:28.040
Oh, not to worry.

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:31.280
Professor Hicks's defensive
magic is superb.

00:01:32.080 --> 00:01:33.320
Until next time.

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:34.880
(chuckles) Such a flatterer.

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:37.640
Well, not really. It is superb.

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:39.600
(Newt) Albus!

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:41.440
I was just wondering...

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:42.680
Ah.

00:01:43.880 --> 00:01:44.840
Yes.

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:47.800
-The case. -Yes.

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:50.600
Rest assured, it's in safe hands.

00:01:55.760 --> 00:01:56.920
(cable car bell dings)

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:02.760
-(door opens) -(bell jingles)

00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:04.960
Can I help you?

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:07.040
(smacks lips) Yes.

00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:09.880
I'd like to have this
case replicated, please.

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:11.440
Certainly.

00:02:13.160 --> 00:02:16.040
Oh. No, you mustn't open it.

00:02:16.360 --> 00:02:20.000
Um, I mean, it's not necessary.

00:02:20.680 --> 00:02:22.600
The interior isn't important.
(chuckles lightly)

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:26.840
I see no reason I can't make you
one.

00:02:33.080 --> 00:02:34.440
(trills softly)

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:40.600
If you leave it here.

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:42.000
Oh. No...

00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:44.480
I couldn't leave it.

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:47.880
And I'll be needing more than one.

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:50.280
You see, um... (sighs)

00:02:51.320 --> 00:02:54.680
...my husband, (chuckles)
he's a bit absentminded.

00:02:54.760 --> 00:02:56.600
He's always forgetting things.

00:02:56.680 --> 00:02:58.600
Just the other day, he
forgot he was married to me.

00:02:58.680 --> 00:02:59.840
(laughs)

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:03.320
Can you imagine? (laughing)

00:03:07.160 --> 00:03:08.840
But I love him.

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:12.280
Exactly how many were you thinking?

00:03:12.360 --> 00:03:13.720
Um...

00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:15.160
Half a dozen,

00:03:15.240 --> 00:03:17.800
and I'll need them in two days'
time.

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:24.520
(suspenseful music playing)

00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:27.680
(wizard) Show your hands.

00:03:32.840 --> 00:03:34.000
Who are you?

00:03:34.840 --> 00:03:36.560
My name is Yusuf Kama.

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:39.600
(Grindelwald) Who's our visitor?

00:03:39.680 --> 00:03:40.960
(Yusuf) I'm an admirer.

00:03:41.640 --> 00:03:43.640
(Rosier) You murdered his sister.

00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:46.280
Her name was Leta.

00:03:47.960 --> 00:03:49.520
Leta Lestrange.

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:51.680
Ah, yes.

00:03:51.760 --> 00:03:53.840
You and your sister share
an ancient bloodline.

00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:55.280
Shared.

00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:57.160
That's the only thing we shared.

00:03:58.360 --> 00:04:01.480
Dumbledore sent you, am I right?

00:04:02.240 --> 00:04:04.480
He fears you're in
possession of a creature.

00:04:05.240 --> 00:04:07.320
He fears the use you may put it to.

00:04:08.240 --> 00:04:10.360
He sent me here to spy on you.

00:04:12.320 --> 00:04:14.320
What would you like me to tell him?

00:04:16.960 --> 00:04:18.080
Queenie.

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:21.400
Is he telling the truth?

00:04:33.680 --> 00:04:34.920
What else?

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:36.760
(Queenie) Even though
he believes in you,

00:04:36.840 --> 00:04:39.520
he holds you responsible
for his sister's death.

00:04:41.160 --> 00:04:43.360
He carries her absence
with him every day.

00:04:45.080 --> 00:04:48.160
Every breath he takes is a reminder
that she breathes no more.

00:04:49.880 --> 00:04:51.240
Then I presume you won't mind

00:04:51.320 --> 00:04:53.240
if I relieve you of
your sister's memory.

00:04:58.480 --> 00:04:59.600
Right?

00:05:00.680 --> 00:05:01.840
Right.

00:05:06.040 --> 00:05:07.480
(strained grunting)

00:05:07.560 --> 00:05:09.320
(shuddering)

00:05:22.840 --> 00:05:23.920
There.

00:05:25.400 --> 00:05:26.920
Better?

00:05:28.120 --> 00:05:29.560
I thought so.

00:05:29.640 --> 00:05:31.800
When we allow ourselves
to be consumed

00:05:31.840 --> 00:05:33.880
by anger, the only
victim is ourself.

00:05:36.280 --> 00:05:38.880
Now, we were just about to depart.

00:05:38.960 --> 00:05:40.680
Perhaps you'd like to join us?

00:05:41.320 --> 00:05:45.480
Come, we can talk some more about
our mutual friend, Dumbledore.

00:05:53.880 --> 00:05:55.200
After you.

00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:11.760
(passersby chattering)

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:17.920
(uneasy music playing)

00:06:27.280 --> 00:06:29.600
(suspenseful music playing)

00:06:48.320 --> 00:06:50.240
(wind whistling)

00:06:53.680 --> 00:06:55.040
(blowing)

00:07:00.560 --> 00:07:02.480
(magical music playing)

00:07:12.320 --> 00:07:13.680
(fizzling)

00:07:19.400 --> 00:07:21.000
Hello, Credence.

00:07:28.040 --> 00:07:31.800
Do you know what it's
like to have no one?

00:07:31.880 --> 00:07:33.960
To always be alone?

00:07:35.200 --> 00:07:36.400
It's you.

00:07:39.240 --> 00:07:42.080
You're the one sending
messages in the mirror.

00:07:43.280 --> 00:07:44.920
I'm a Dumbledore.

00:07:45.560 --> 00:07:47.440
You abandoned me.

00:07:48.840 --> 00:07:52.720
The same blood that runs
my veins runs yours.

00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:04.080
He's not here for you.

00:08:04.160 --> 00:08:05.640
He's here for me.

